'''wheat-bird''' (hwēt′bėrd), ''n.'' The chaffinch or wheatsel-bird. [Local, British.]

'''wheat-brush''' (hwēt′brush), ''n.'' In ''milling,'' a grain-scouring machine. {{smaller|It consists essentially of two brushes in the form of disks placed close together in a hopper, one brush remaining stationary, and the other revolving rapidly as the grain is delivered between them. The grain is carried to the periphery of the brushes by centrifugal force, and falls into a chamber beneath, whence}}
